<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 535 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 535 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 535 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 91 million stg outright in bills and 444 million stg in repos to August 12 and 13.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 915 million stg so far on Wednesday, in response to a revised forecast money market shortage of 2.15 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
